            "target_entity_instance": "Temperature",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "Figure 1. Climate change-robust machine learning. Deep learning models trained on historical climatic conditions face a distribution shift when applied to future climate projections. In this paper we consider models that predict plant phenological dates from meteorological time series and devise a domain adaptation method to enhance their robustness to such shifts. (Temperature data: CMIP6 CNRM-CM6-1 SSP2-4.5 [12, 38], phenological data: Swiss Phenology Network [13])",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
